repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/digger32/Evaluation-protocol-for-tabular-foundation-models
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of a significance-, stability- and calibration-aware
  evaluation protocol for tabular systems: a job-based benchmark runner that
  writes one record per dataset, split policy, model and seed; an analysis stage
  that scores point metrics, proper scoring rules and calibration together with
  paired tests, bootstrap intervals and resampling-based rank-stability bands;
  and a review-proofing gate of eleven assertions that refuses to release numbers
  whose provenance cannot be checked. The repository also carries the released
  run behind the accompanying article: 6,395 per-cell records, the run manifest
  and the twelve analysis outputs.
keywords:
